- ### Finding the annotated field
+ ### Das annotierte Feld finden

- Often the question runs the other way: *which* field carries the annotation? When exactly one
- field does, the summoned instance knows its name:
+ Oft lautet die Frage umgekehrt: *Welches* Feld trägt die Annotation? Wenn genau ein Feld sie trägt,
+ kennt die herbeigerufene Instanz seinen Namen:

= field does, the summoned instance knows its name:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= field does, the summoned instance knows its name:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= field does, the summoned instance knows its name:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(summon[Speech is Annotated by primary].field)
+ Out.println(summon[Speech is Annotated by primary].field)

= Out.println(summon[Speech is Annotated by primary].field)
- ```
+ ```

- Finding the field is usually the first step towards reading or writing it, so the instance also
- offers a [lens](optics.md#lenses-as-values) onto it:
+ Das Feld zu finden ist meist der erste Schritt, um es zu lesen oder zu schreiben, daher bietet die
+ Instanz auch eine [Linse](optics.md#lenses-as-values) darauf:

= offers a [lens](optics.md#lenses-as-values) onto it:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
+ val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")

= val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
- ```
+ ```

= val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- val identity = summon[Person is Annotated by ident]
+ val identity = summon[Person is Annotated by ident]

- Out.println(identity.lens(person))
+ Out.println(identity.lens(person))

- Out.println(identity.lens.update(person, t"juliet@example.com").inspect)
+ Out.println(identity.lens.update(person, t"juliet@example.com").inspect)

= Out.println(identity.lens.update(person, t"juliet@example.com").inspect)
- ```
+ ```

- This is how a serialization library finds "the field marked as the identifier" without being
- told its name. If more than one field carries the annotation, `field` is not available, because
- the type of the instance records whether the match was unique.
+ So findet eine Serialisierungsbibliothek „das als Bezeichner markierte Feld“, ohne dass man ihr
+ seinen Namen nennt. Trägt mehr als ein Feld die Annotation, ist `field` nicht verfügbar, denn der
+ Typ der Instanz hält fest, ob der Treffer eindeutig war.

